From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:01:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/47] perf(canvas): show frame pictures in place of live
 documents while the zoom moves

Off by default; localStorage['doop:zoom-pictures'] = 'on' plus a reload switches it on.

Every step of a zoom changes each live frame's scale, so the frames' renderer re-rasters every
document on every step. With the switch on, the first zoom step of a gesture (a pure pan does not
count) shows each live frame's preview picture (the one patch 0009 mounts, at its usePreviewLevel /
previewSrc, sharpPreviews included) and hides its iframe with visibility: hidden. The iframe stays
mounted, so nothing reloads. When the camera settles (the 250 ms layout-zoom settle, plus a frame,
so the new pixel density rasters once, under the picture) the documents are shown again first, and
each picture is hidden only after its runtime answers doop:painted (two animation frames), so
nothing flashes. A new gesture before that answer keeps the picture up.

A frame keeps its document when:
- its picture has not loaded (never a blank image), or the document has not shown yet
- it is selected, or an element in it is picked
- it is being edited inline, or a path in it is being edited
- it is moved, resized, rotated, or a shape or element in it is moving
- an agent is streaming into it, or a peer has it active
- Prototype mode is on
- it is a standalone canvas element
A frame registers only while none of these hold; leaving mid-gesture gives its document back at
once. A frame that registers mid-gesture is left alone until the next gesture.

The writes touch only the swapped frames' iframe and picture wrapper: at gesture start one style
recalc of 34 elements (0.7-0.9 ms), at the end two of 12 elements (0.4-1.1 ms).

Measured on a page of 6 live frames, perf/trace-pinch.mjs + raster.mjs, swiftshader, two
interleaved rounds off/on (counts; load 7.3 falling to 2.7):
- frames-process RasterTask: B1 309/320 -> 30/25, B2 306/334 -> 26/26, all of them after rest
- tiles per frame document layer (B1): 68-78 in 23-25 raster frames -> 5-7 in 2-3
- frames-process compositor busy: B1 288/352 -> 45/32 ms, B2 288/331 -> 47/33 ms
- editor main thread busy: B1 415/450 -> 347/360 ms, B2 462/519 -> 353/399 ms
- editor RasterTask rises (B1 89 -> 137, B2 166 -> 209): the picture layers, under 1 ms each
At rest the stage is pixel-identical on and off; a screencast after the last zoom step shows no
frame off the settled view.

Off, the behaviour is unchanged: no picture stays mounted under a shown document.

